KG42.register("clusters-790f28402bbd331cc1a3c907",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v142-d-CL001","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","label":"Supply-and-demand-information-driven local bilateral transaction clearing and pricing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Supply-and-demand-information-driven local bilateral transaction clearing and pricing","market_meaning":"Taking participants' surplus renewable energy and demand information as inputs, the aggregator organizes matching and clearing, and assembles the buyer's energy-purchase decisions, transaction feasibility, and the bilateral transaction volumes and prices generated by equilibrium into candidate rules. Competition under shortage and seller-selection behavior under surplus are retained separately as case conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","activation","matching","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The general model, the shortage periods and surplus periods of Case 3 apply separately; different supply-demand conditions cannot be combined into a priority allocation rule that holds simultaneously. The assumed price change in R005 is retained as a case-competition explanation; the clause in R004 prohibiting simultaneous buying and selling retains the 5.1 test configuration scope. The TLOU upper limit has not yet been equated with the buyer's load-related electricity price.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"These Rule-Chains revolve around the same bilateral energy transaction and respectively provide product scope, supply and demand information, energy-purchase objectives, matching responsibilities, feasible transaction volumes, and endogenous prices, with explicit information and quantity interfaces. Participation withdrawal, SES intertemporal response, and cost accounting have independent results, are placed in separate Rule-Clusters, and retain connections through shared references.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Determine the scope of energy products entering the supply side of this Rule-Cluster, without creating separate product variables."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the aggregator's responsibility for collecting supply and demand information; the SES operation responsibility is retained at the same time and cited as background in the energy-storage response Rule-Cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the buyer's cost objective for choosing P2P and grid energy purchases, as well as transaction permission and execution restrictions with source scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the aggregator's matching responsibility and counterparty selection in the surplus-supply case, while retaining its case conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the aggregator's clearing responsibility, transaction-volume feasibility, and buyer energy balance; the shortage-allocation description is retained as a case explanation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the output relationship between equilibrium transaction volumes and endogenous prices and the existing price bounds, without treating its abbreviated expression as a complete equilibrium-solving system."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-Ps","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"rationale":"The product Rule-Chain defines surplus renewable energy, and the seller clearing constraint limits the energy that can be sold in the same market; the two respectively provide the qualitative nature and quantitative boundary of supply, and the product node is not equated with a supply parameter."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e010"],"rationale":"The citation explicitly states that the aggregator collects supply and demand information and clears this P2P market, supporting the assembly of information collection and clearing activities; this mapping does not add submission timing or information-integrity constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p_sb","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p_bg","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-psb","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbg","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e028"],"rationale":"The buyer objective and energy balance use the same buyer, time period, and bilateral purchase quantity; the source text also explicitly specifies consistency between the buyer's and seller's transaction variables. Here, the energy-purchase objective is connected to feasibility without rewriting the variable roles of each Rule-Chain."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-psb","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"The same bilateral transaction volume is both constrained by seller supply and buyer balance and is an equilibrium output; this interface does not mean that the complete KKT conditions are included in the frozen Rule-Chain."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-rho"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that the same P2P price is endogenous in the overall equilibrium and serves as a parameter when deriving an individual participant's conditions. The distinct local roles of the execution-side parameter and the equilibrium-side variable are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g03-e14","v141-b-g03-e15"],"rationale":"The matching responsibility and equilibrium output target bilateral transactions in the same market; the t = 15 low-price seller-selection explanation supplements the surplus-supply condition, and the assumed price change cannot be used to grant the seller unilateral authority to control the equilibrium price."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e003"],"rationale":"The aggregator in the citations simultaneously bears information collection, clearing, and matching responsibilities, and the three references point to the same institutional node. The representative selection is for display only and does not merge its different activities or edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E23"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the clearing function of this local P2P market that determines transaction volumes and prices; the original constraints and relationships remain independently traceable."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g03-e12","v141-b-g03-e13","v141-b-g03-e14","v141-b-g03-e15"],"rationale":"The general pricing mechanism and the Case 3 explanation reference the same local pricing function; node identity does not mean that price values for different bilateral transactions or time periods are the same, nor does it merge case-condition edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-psb","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p_sb","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e028"],"rationale":"The source definition and the statement of consistency between buyer and seller variables support the association of the same bilateral transaction quantity; all three local roles—clearing-feasible quantity, buyer energy-purchase decision, and equilibrium allocation quantity—are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbg","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p_bg"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The grid energy-purchase quantity for the same buyer and time period is used respectively in the cost objective and the energy balance; the two local objects are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-rho","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"The explicit endogenous price and the treatment of participant KKT parameters support the quantity-identity association; the execution-side parameter and the overall equilibrium variable cannot be rewritten as one object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-Delta_t","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"Both use the time-period length of this multi-period model, but they respectively serve energy-purchase cost and price decomposition; the original parameter references remain independent."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence used by this Rule-Cluster remains unverified and only has candidate-support eligibility for this experiment; no B-source audit, C2 independent review, or E review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g03-e13","v141-b-g03-e14","v141-b-g03-e15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the relevant source text, formulas, and case scope before judging scientific validity; this round does not change the evidence status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The frozen catalog does not include the seller's complete profit objective or the complete constraints of equilibrium (26) and the KKT system (28)–(45). The dual quantities in the R008 price expression are also not declared in this Rule-Chain's variable or parameter catalog; its two clauses containing price decomposition cannot replace the complete equilibrium system.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g02-e029","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e033","v141-b-g02-e034"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should complete the seller objective, equilibrium conditions, and dual-quantity definitions and bindings according to the source text, and check their applicability conditions; D keeps the existing expressions and objects unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The buyer balance includes SES charging and discharging, but the frozen Rule-Chain has not yet provided a complete mathematical closure for energy-storage state evolution, energy bounds, shared-capacity allocation, and fairness conditions. The related node proposals remain pending decision, and the aggregator's operation responsibility cannot fill in these constraints.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbc","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbd","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g02-e025","v141-b-g02-e027"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-X01","v141-b-g01-X02","v141-b-g02-p001"],"required_work":"Manually process the pending ontology proposals, and upstream should additionally record the applicable energy-storage physics, capacity-sharing, and normalized equilibrium conditions; before that, do not claim that a complete energy-storage allocation or fairness mechanism has been assembled."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The TLOU in the price ceiling has no explicit index and cannot be directly identified as the buyer grid electricity price in R004. Candidate transcriptions also differ in how the buyer index is written, and the frozen Rule-Chain does not include the complete electricity-price definition relationship of equation (7).","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_buy","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-TLOU","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g03-e04"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-X03"],"required_work":"Check the electricity-price index, load-dependency relationship, ceiling convention, and applicable quantifiers; decide the quantity mapping only after clarifying the external electricity-price proposal, and currently keep the references distinct."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Equation (7) makes the grid electricity price depend on the purchased quantity; substituting it into the buyer objective produces a quadratic energy-purchase cost, and equation (33) also has a corresponding marginal term. The candidate citation calls the participant problem an LP; merely treating the P2P price as a parameter is not sufficient to confirm that the buyer objective is linear or that a complete MILP transformation holds.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_buy","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e033"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the convexity of the actual objective, the necessity and sufficiency of KKT, and the conditions required for transformation, and complete the upstream mathematical records; do not rewrite the frozen objective or price formula in order to eliminate doubts."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G006","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The assumed seller price change in R005 and the equilibrium endogenous price in R008 are at different narrative levels; the prohibition on simultaneous buying and selling in R004 comes from the test configuration. The existing materials do not establish a general bidding protocol, nor do they state whether this test restriction applies to all model situations.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g03-e15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm whether the case price change is only a counterfactual competition explanation and the scope of application of the test prohibition condition; retain the shortage, surplus, and test-configuration conditions, and do not derive new bidding rights or matching algorithms from the narrative."}]},"rule_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R009","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R002","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R004","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R005","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3cc1c6ed2324280e","COMP-3fcd5e2d02ec7c3f","COMP-4c1817f6cddf8a9c","COMP-58a3c8caf66a5d40","COMP-5ed84d11cdfb4465","COMP-820ecd8f4d709ac7","COMP-d063772d8846dd91","COMP-da34359f040da554","COMP-e49253a62f66ee53"]});
